  <ym-title|Two-regime paid estimate for a regular
  source><label|two-regime-paid-estimate-for-a-regular-source>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, selected-scale trace producer.

    <item>Status: draft; numerical two-regime conversion is proved from
    explicit local chart, cloud, format, density, and remainder receipts. The
    local chart receipts are not claimed to follow from the numerical budget
    inequalities.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-regular-atom.tex>.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source crosswalk><label|source-crosswalk>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  content>>|<cell|<strong|Exact declaration and path>>|<cell|<strong|Checked
  correspondence and remaining status>>>|<row|<cell|Regular atom and cost
  target>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.salary>,
  <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.PaidAtom>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/SOURCE_HISTORIES/LocalDebt.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|salary>
  is one supported masked regular source. <verbatim|PaidAtom> requires, for
  each motion, a coefficient close to the predicted lead, a predecessor
  coefficient with format and remainder control, and equality of its density
  to the pushed transformed fine source. The manuscript states the one-source
  conclusion in ordinary mathematical terms.>>|<row|<cell|Constructing the
  regular local certificate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.salaryT>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Graces.regularCard>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Graces.sendsCard>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Nick.atom_lead>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Soil.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Elder.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Cloudlet.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Attar.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|salaryT>
  takes an input <verbatim|RegFit> source on support <verbatim|b>, its
  sup-bound <verbatim|c>, the exact next-level history, a <verbatim|Medal>, a
  <verbatim|Bunk>, and the selected <verbatim|Moms>, <verbatim|Cruise>,
  <verbatim|Arrives>, budget, and geometry hypotheses. Its mass is the
  fine-level mass <verbatim|exp(fine supportExponent * fine cover(b))*c>.
  <verbatim|regularCard> creates the local insertion certificate;
  <verbatim|sendsCard> converts its reserved-mass and turn-price bounds to
  the remainder cost; <verbatim|Nick.atom_lead> converts that certificate to
  the <verbatim|PaidAtom> definition. Raw Bunk budgets become actual sprite
  prices after division by the positive <verbatim|coinP(G,L,beta)>.>>|<row|<cell|Small
  support branch>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.mire>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.ribbonW>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Mire.lean>,
  <verbatim|Creel.lean>>|<cell|If the transported support cover is at most
  the coarse budget radius, <verbatim|mire> gives local-chart regularity and
  ordered derivative/probe bounds. <verbatim|ribbonW> compares the total row
  to the distinguished row with two readout terms, one for each real channel.
  The probe term is Wu<em|m0/chi. The cloud terms are Ha>(C1+C2), with each
  Ci \<less\>= (v/chi)*m0.>>|<row|<cell|Large support
  branch>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.desert>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.Medal.talent>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Day.lean>,
  <verbatim|Guild.lean>>|<cell|If the cover exceeds the coarse radius,
  <verbatim|desert> uses the scale/cover construction and the Medal's
  one-site talent field to get chart bounds Si \<less\>= (v/chi)<em|m0.
  Separately, the Medal cloud field gives Ci \<less\>= (v/chi)<em|m0. The
  source error is O>H>a*(S1+S2+C1+C2), hence at most
  4<em|O>H<em|a>v*m0/chi.>>|<row|<cell|Cloud and reserved-mass
  bounds>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.Medal.cloud>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Graces.crowning>, <verbatim|attestCard>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Guild.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/RG_NEXT_COMPLETE_REPEATABLE_NONLINEAR_STEP/Graces/Momentum.lean>,
  <verbatim|Graces/Aspire.lean>, <verbatim|Graces/Eagles.lean>>|<cell|The
  Medal cloud field bounds each channel's weighted cloud quantity by the
  sprite price times its source mass. The parent manuscript's
  <verbatim|sec:regular-principal-producer> proves the three support-regime
  estimates used by <verbatim|crowning>; this chapter cross-references it
  rather than duplicating it. The support/ticket conversion and exact
  one-site assignment are supplied by <verbatim|attestCard>/<verbatim|sendsCard>.>>|<row|<cell|Bunk
  budget inputs>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.Bunk>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Cache.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|reg>
  is (O(Wu+2Hav)\\le\\xi), and <verbatim|huge> is (4OHav\\le\\xi). The
  <verbatim|cycle> field pays the local coefficient variation needed for the
  small-support probes. These inequalities alone do not prove the local chart
  receipts.>>|<row|<cell|Actual producer route>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.Cashbox>,
  <verbatim|.mosaic>, <verbatim|.salaryT>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Soot.lean>, <verbatim|Kiosk.lean>,
  <verbatim|Soil.lean>>|<cell|The selected <verbatim|Stepper> regular field
  is <verbatim|salaryT> and is reached through
  <verbatim|Cashbox>/<verbatim|mosaic>. The proof depends on the actual
  adjacent history, not a detached one-step interface. The primary and forced
  branches are separate fields (<verbatim|primaryT>, <verbatim|gasT>).>>>>>

  <section|Checks and open obligations><label|checks-and-open-obligations>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Read-only source inspection: <verbatim|sed -n> on
    <verbatim|LocalDebt.lean>, <verbatim|Chalet.lean>, <verbatim|Attar.lean>,
    <verbatim|Elder.lean>, <verbatim|Cloudlet.lean>, <verbatim|Creel.lean>,
    <verbatim|Mire.lean>, <verbatim|Day.lean>, <verbatim|Soil.lean>,
    <verbatim|Guild.lean>, <verbatim|Cache.lean>, <verbatim|Soot.lean>, and
    <verbatim|Kiosk.lean>; <verbatim|rg -n> to locate exact declaration paths
    and callers.

    <item>Read-only parent manuscript inspection:
    <verbatim|manuscript/existence/regular-principal-producer.tex>, section
    <verbatim|sec:regular-principal-producer>;
    <verbatim|primary-calibration-producer.tex>, section
    <verbatim|sec:primary-calibration-producer>, to avoid duplicating already
    drafted principal/primary arguments.

    <item>No Lean source was edited; no Lean or TeX build was run.

    <item>The numerical two-regime implication is proved here. Remaining
    review scope is checking the detailed mathematical correspondence of the
    local chart and reserved-mass receipts to their source proofs;
    <verbatim|mire>, <verbatim|desert>, <verbatim|regularCard>, and
    <verbatim|salaryT> are not replaced by names alone in the article, but
    their complete geometric derivations are not reproduced in this bounded
    chapter.
  </itemize-minus>

